ce":0.456,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Joe Lombardi"},{"season":2023,"team":"GB","distance":0.4868,"shared":15,"play_caller":"Matt LaFleur"},{"season":2018,"team":"MIN","distance":0.4936,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2018,"team":"CIN","distance":0.5153,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2018,"team":"MIA","distance":0.6527,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"GB","distance":0.6546,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2018,"team":"SF","distance":0.7223,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Robert Saleh"},{"season":2022,"team":"SF","distance":0.7427,"shared":18,"play_caller":"DeMeco Ryans"},{"season":2023,"team":"CAR","distance":0.7807,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Ejiro Evero"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Seahawks went 12-4 in 2020 and outscored opponents 459 to 371. The offense ranked 11th in EPA per play and the defense 17th in EPA allowed, so neither side stood out much. What set them apart was a pass rate over expected that was among the highest and the 3rd lowest two-high safety rate in the league.","offense":"The Seahawks offense was a little above average by EPA per play. They threw more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score did not call for it. Their biggest outliers in how they lined up were the 3rd highest 12 personnel usage in the league. Russell Wilson ran the passing game, with Tyler Lockett leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Seahawks defense was about average by EPA allowed per play. It was much better against the run than the pass, ranking 5th and 21st. Jamal Adams led the team with 9.5 sacks, and Jarran Reed added 6.5, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. In terms of scheme, they had the 3rd lowest two-high safety rate in the league.","special":"The Seahawks were one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 18% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers made 100% of field goals, which was the best in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into tight ends, about 7% of the money on the books. Their running backs were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Russell Wilson played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 4,212 yards. Tyler Lockett was the clear top target with 25% of the looks and 1,054 receiving yards. The backfield was a committee led by Chris Carson and Carlos Hyde. On defense, Jamal Adams led the team with 9.5 sacks and Quandre Diggs picked off 5 passes.","coaching":"Brian Schottenheimer called the offense, and the defensive play caller for this season is not in the coaching data. Their offense looked most like the 2024 Texans under Bobby Slowik and the 2021 Chargers under Joe Lombardi. Their defense looked most like the 2018 Dolphins and the 2025 Packers.","trends":"The offense went from 12th in EPA per play in 2019 to 11th in 2020, about where it was. The defense moved from 19th in EPA allowed per play in 2019 to 17th in 2020, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was 12 personnel usage, which went from 15% to 31%.","notes":"FTN did not start charting plays until 2022, so play action, motion, RPO and screen rates are not available for 2020. Everything else, including personnel, formations and coverage, is complete for this season."}}